  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The circumference of a circle is \\(100\\) inches. The side of a square inscribed in this circle, expressed in inches, is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{25\\sqrt2}{\\pi}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{50\\sqrt2}{\\pi}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{100}{\\pi}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{100\\sqrt2}{\\pi}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(50\\sqrt2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1960-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The diameter is \\(\\frac{100}{\\pi}.\\) If the square has side \\(s,\\) its diagonal is \\(s\\sqrt2,\\) so \\[ s\\sqrt2=\\frac{100}{\\pi}. \\] Therefore \\(s=\\frac{50\\sqrt2}{\\pi}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Find the diameter from the circumference",
        "The diagonal of the inscribed square is the circle’s diameter"
      ],
